## Project conventions

{{PROJECT_CONVENTIONS}}

## MUST / MUST NOT

- **Never** commit secrets: `.env`, tokens, API keys, credentials.
- **Commits**: Conventional Commits 1.0.0 — `feat|fix|docs|refactor|perf|test|build|ci|chore(scope): description`. Use `docs(internal): …` for internal plans or research docs.
- **Issues**: use `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/` forms when present; never open title-only issues.
- **Pull requests**: follow `.github/pull_request_template.md` when present; link the issue (`Closes #…`).
- Follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) and the label taxonomy in [`.github/labels.md`](.github/labels.md) when present.
- **Modularity**: small, cohesive units with minimal coupling; extract shared logic instead of copy-pasting.
{{#IF_RELEASE_MODEL}}

## Branching & releases

Read [`RELEASING.md`](RELEASING.md) before branching, opening a PR, or releasing. It is the source of truth for trunk, maintenance branches, and backports. Never merge one long-lived branch into another to sync it.
{{/IF_RELEASE_MODEL}}
